  "note": "Triennial election, January 1926 (poll 15 January). The North and South-West wards were uncontested; six candidates stood for the four South-East seats. South-West Ward: returned unopposed. David Rock: no party label printed in 1926. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Portadown, Armagh County Council, 26 May 1927, printed 'U': Armagh Guardian, 3 June 1927, p. 3 (\"New Co. Council: Portadown Apathy in Voting\"); Lurgan Mail, 4 June 1927, p. 4 (\"County Armagh Election\")). His labels elsewhere differ (UUP x1, Labour Unionist x1). John Davison: no party label printed in 1926. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Armagh, Parliament of Northern Ireland, 25 November 1925, listed as Unionist; Mid Armagh, Parliament of Northern Ireland, 22 May 1929, listed as Unionist)."
